students have the same family story, or must share it, ignores privacy and different circumstances. Correct the claim or use of sources, not just the neatness of the poster.","title":"Test a misconception"},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use the same HSIE idea on a new place, person, source or context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy of evidence. Supported records follow the actual sources and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence.","options":["Use the same HSIE idea on a new place, person, source or context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy of evidence.","A claim unrelated to the source or place.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no evidence."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about origin?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nAustralians'' families come from First Nations Peoples and from many countries around the world. A family origin map uses pins and a key to show places that are part of a family story. People choose what to share, and some families prefer to share a place that is special to them. Now choose a different example to show you can transfer the idea.\n\nTRY FIRST\nInquire into or describe one fresh example that uses the same skill and write a short evidence-based reason.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe new example should use the same HSIE idea as the model, but contain different evidence.","explain":"Use the same HSIE idea on a new place, person, source or context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy of evidence.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner base claims on sources, places and respectful community knowledge, rather than guessing from a single picture. Keep every claim linked to evidence.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a detail is uncertain, identify what source you would need next. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new evidence. Correct the claim or use of sources, not just the neatness of the poster.","title":"Transfer to a new inquiry"}],"title":"Year 3, Week 31, Lesson 2: Where our families come from","unit_number":7,"unit_title":"Cultures and communities","week":31,"week_in_unit":1,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nExample: a student places pins on a world map: one for where a grandparent was born, one for where their family lives now and one for a place their family often visits. The key says pin colours and the student writes two facts about each.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the sources, places or community details used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"A family origin map.","caption":"Use a key for pin colours.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Pin</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">where a grandparent was born</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Pin</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">where we live now</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Privacy on family maps.","caption":"No one has to share.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Choice</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">share if you wish</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Special place</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">a place that matters</text></g></svg>"}],"year_level":"Year 3"}') WHERE seed_key='s2-hsie-y3-w31-l2' AND family_id IS NULL;
